  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts and it passes typecheck. I haven't run `vite build` or looked at a rendered frame, so the lighting and framing are untested.\n\n- **Robot:** it is built from primitives as nested groups, so each joint rotates everything below it. It has 11 articulated joints: hips, chest, head, two shoulders, two elbows, two hips (legs) and two knees.\n- **Animation:** the `onFrame` callback drives the idle motion. It breathes, shifts weight side to side, and moves the head and arms gently, so frames differ over time.\n- **Lighting:**\n  - The background is near-black.\n  - A strong warm key light casts shadows onto a grey floor.\n  - A magenta rim light and a blue rim light sit behind the robot.\n- **Camera:** a perspective camera looks at the robot's centre from the front.\n- **Contract:** it draws into `#app` and renders continuously. `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after the first frame.\n\nThe scene is adapted from the repo's `procedural-humanoid` recipe in `docs/agents/recipes-src/`.",
